UPDATE legal_pages SET content = $$<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2><p>We collect information you provide directly to us when you book an appointment, request a consultation, fill out a contact form, or visit our clinic. This may include your name, phone number, email address, age, medical and dental history, and any details you share about your treatment needs.</p><h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2><ul><li>Provide and improve dental care, treatment planning, and follow-up</li><li>Schedule, confirm, and remind you of appointments</li><li>Respond to your enquiries, consultations, and dental tourism requests</li><li>Maintain accurate medical and billing records as required by law</li><li>Send important updates, offers, or oral-health information (only if you opt in)</li></ul><h2>3. How We Protect Your Information</h2><p>All patient records are stored on secure, access-controlled systems. Only authorised clinical and administrative staff can view your data. Digital records are encrypted in transit and at rest, and physical files are kept in restricted areas of the clinic.</p><h2>4. Sharing of Information</h2><p>We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information. We may share limited information with:</p><ul><li>Specialists or laboratories directly involved in your treatment</li><li>Insurance providers (only with your consent)</li><li>Government or regulatory bodies when legally required</li></ul><h2>5. Cookies & Website Analytics</h2><p>Our website uses essential cookies to function properly and analytics tools to understand how visitors use the site. You can disable cookies in your browser settings at any time. We do not use cookies to identify you personally.</p><h2>6. Patient Photos & Testimonials</h2><p>Before-and-after photos, video testimonials, and reviews are only published with your explicit written consent. You can withdraw consent at any time by contacting us.</p><h2>7. Your Rights</h2><ul><li>Request access to the personal information we hold about you</li><li>Ask us to correct or update inaccurate information</li><li>Request deletion of your records (subject to legal retention requirements)</li><li>Opt out of marketing communications at any time</li></ul><h2>8. Contact Us</h2><p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy or how your data is handled, please contact us via the email and phone listed on our Contact page.</p>$$ WHERE slug='privacy';

UPDATE legal_pages SET content = $$<h2>1. Acceptance of Terms</h2><p>By accessing our website, booking an appointment, or receiving treatment at Kundalini Dental Clinic, you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service and our Privacy Policy.</p><h2>2. Services Provided</h2><p>We provide dental and oral healthcare services including consultations, preventive care, restorative treatments, cosmetic dentistry, orthodontics, implants, and dental tourism coordination. All treatments are performed by licensed dental professionals.</p><h2>3. Appointments & Cancellations</h2><ul><li>Appointments can be booked online, by phone, or in person.</li><li>We require at least 24 hours' notice for cancellations or rescheduling.</li><li>Late arrivals may result in a shortened appointment or rescheduling.</li><li>Repeated no-shows may require a non-refundable deposit for future bookings.</li></ul><h2>4. Treatment Consent</h2><p>All major treatments require informed written consent. Our clinicians will explain the procedure, risks, alternatives, and expected outcomes before obtaining your consent. You may withdraw consent at any time before treatment begins.</p><h2>5. Pricing & Payment</h2><ul><li>Prices listed online are starting estimates and may vary based on individual diagnosis.</li><li>A formal treatment plan with final pricing is provided after consultation.</li><li>We accept cash, card, bank transfer, and major digital payment methods.</li><li>For multi-stage treatments, payment may be split into agreed milestones.</li></ul><h2>6. Dental Tourism Patients</h2><p>International patients are responsible for their own travel, visa, and accommodation arrangements unless explicitly included in a tourism package. Treatment timelines provided are estimates and may change based on clinical findings.</p><h2>7. Website Use</h2><p>Content on this website is for informational purposes only and is not a substitute for professional dental advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Always consult a qualified dentist for personalised advice.</p><h2>8. Limitation of Liability</h2><p>We strive to deliver the highest standard of care, but treatment outcomes may vary based on individual biology, compliance with aftercare, and underlying conditions. Our liability is limited to the cost of the specific treatment provided.</p><h2>9. Changes to These Terms</h2><p>We may update these Terms of Service from time to time. Material changes will be posted on this page with an updated revision date.</p><h2>10. Contact</h2><p>Questions about these terms? Reach us via the contact details on our Contact page.</p>$$ WHERE slug='terms';

UPDATE legal_pages SET content = $$<h2>1. Consultation Fees</h2><p>Initial consultation fees are non-refundable once the consultation has taken place. If you cancel at least 24 hours in advance, the fee can be applied as credit toward a future appointment within 90 days.</p><h2>2. Treatment Deposits</h2><ul><li>Deposits secure your treatment slot, lab work, and materials.</li><li>Cancellations more than 14 days before treatment: 80% refund of deposit.</li><li>Cancellations 7–14 days before treatment: 50% refund.</li><li>Cancellations within 7 days of treatment: deposit is non-refundable as lab work and materials have already been ordered.</li></ul><h2>3. Completed Treatments</h2><p>Payments for completed dental procedures are non-refundable. If you experience any clinical issue with your treatment, please contact us immediately — we offer complimentary review appointments and stand behind the quality of our work with applicable warranties.</p><h2>4. Multi-Stage Treatments</h2><p>For treatments paid in stages (e.g. orthodontics, full-mouth rehabilitation, implants), refunds for incomplete stages are calculated based on the work already performed and any lab/material costs incurred. A detailed breakdown will be provided.</p><h2>5. Dental Tourism Packages</h2><p>Dental tourism deposits cover treatment planning, slot reservation, and coordination services. Refund eligibility:</p><ul><li>More than 30 days before arrival: 90% refund</li><li>15–30 days before arrival: 50% refund</li><li>Less than 15 days: non-refundable, but may be transferred to a new date within 6 months</li></ul><h2>6. Non-Refundable Items</h2><ul><li>Custom lab work (crowns, veneers, aligners, dentures) once production has begun</li><li>Imaging and diagnostic reports already issued</li><li>Third-party charges (travel, accommodation, visa fees)</li></ul><h2>7. How to Request a Refund</h2><p>To request a refund, please email us using the address on our Contact page with your name, treatment date, and reason for the request. Approved refunds are processed within 7–14 business days using the original payment method.</p><h2>8. Disputes</h2><p>We are committed to resolving any concerns fairly and quickly. Please contact us first so we can work together toward a resolution before pursuing other options.</p>$$ WHERE slug='refund';